      "signature": "GetRootNode(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FXmlFile*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "FXmlNode*",
      "docs": "Returns the root node of the loaded file. nullptr if no file loaded.\nIt is assumed that there will always be one and only one root node.\n@return\t\t\t\t\t\tPointer to root node"
    },
    {
      "id": "save",
      "name": "Save",
      "category": "XmlFile",
      "signature": "Save(Target, Path)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FXmlFile*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Path",
          "type": "String&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "Write to disk, UTF-16 format only at the moment\n@param\tPath\t\t\t\tFile path to save to\n@return\t\t\t\t\t\tWhether writing the XML to a file succeeded"
    },
    {
      "id": "enable-attempt-to-preserve-whitespace-hack",
      "name": "EnableAttemptToPreserveWhitespaceHack",
      "category": "XmlFile",
      "signature": "EnableAttemptToPreserveWhitespaceHack(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FXmlFile*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Turns on a specific hack that is only used by the crash report client in order\nto retain newlines for callstacks. This is important on the server side when we\ndisplay the callstacks to content creators. Without the content-whitespace,\nthey're bascially illegible. Neither version of the DOM we create is technically\ntrue to the XML spec."
    },
